Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a jobsite theft on behalf of our client Beacon Mechanical Services, Inc. Our reference is FRC/IM/2025/7741.

Their controller is away and they could not give us the policy number, so please locate on our reference. This is their combined equipment and installation floater, not the liability policy - it is first-party theft of their own property.

Broker reference: FRC/IM/2025/7741
Insured name: Beacon Mechanical Services, Inc.
Insured trading as: Beacon HVAC & Plumbing
Date of loss: 13 September 2025
Loss location: 19400 East 32nd Parkway, Aurora, CO 80011
Cause: Theft - forced entry to a job trailer and a shared container
Estimated loss: USD 224,300

Someone cut the padlock on our client's job trailer over the weekend and levered
the shared conex. They took the tools with resale value and left the rest, and
they took the copper - which is the part that hurts, because it drives the next
three weeks of their programme.

Two of the scheduled items are gone: the Ridgid threading machine and the roll
groover. Serials are filed with the National Equipment Register.

The loss spans both sections. The tools and the welder are equipment; the copper,
the fittings and the condensing units are installation material going into the
building. The general contractor is asking whether their builder's risk picks up
the copper - our reading is that our client's installation cover sits excess of it.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * theft investigation report
  * schedule of property taken

Please confirm a claim reference. Our client needs your position on the copper
sublimit by Thursday or they slip the riser.

